## Summary

The P9-0001 XCTest unit suite existed but **never compiled or ran** — every iOS/macOS build in this slot died on a deterministic **Swift 6.3.2 IRGen compiler crash**. I root-caused and fixed it, which unblocked the whole suite.

**Root-cause fix (the blocker):** `AppearanceSettings.Controls.swift` passed a `@MainActor (Bool)->Void` closure straight into a `Sendable` `Binding<Bool>` setter, emitting an `@isolated(any) @Sendable` reabstraction thunk that overflows an LLVM SmallVector in IRGen (`report_at_maximum_capacity`). Routed it through `MainActor.assumeIsolated` (behaviour-identical).

**6 latent test errors surfaced once it compiled, all fixed:** 2 internal helper-type collisions (`ChangeSpy`, `SpyStateTimelineTelemetry` → `private`), a non-`@Sendable` global closure, 2 missing `import SwiftUI`, and a wrong FleetCompare battery-highlight expectation (corrected to web parity `"—%"`). Also cleared the **placeholder gate (134→0)** + 3 swiftlint + 1 swiftformat defects.

**Gate results:**
- **iOS — GREEN:** test build SUCCEEDED; **20,690 unit tests, 0 failures**.
- **swiftlint 0 / swiftformat 0 / placeholder 0.**
- **macOS — BLOCKED:** `build test` compiles SUCCESSFULLY then fails code-signing — restricted entitlements need a dev certificate and the host has 0 valid identities (`MAC_EXIT=65`, documented ADR-012 gap, deferred to a signed runner).

Per the gate formula (`MAC_EXIT≠0`), the log records **`EXIT=65 / STATUS=BLOCKED`** — the same unavoidable macOS dev-cert gap as the 3 prior runs, but this run unblocked and greened the entire iOS deliverable (20,690 tests vs the priors that couldn't run the bundle). Committed 65 `apps/apple` source fixes + the gate log (`393a30fa5`).

Coverage: per-parity-unit state coverage recorded (loading 662 / empty 875 / error 702 / stale 510 of 942 surfaces; golden-vector parity passes); fresh per-line xccov deferred with the macOS leg due to host OOM-contention.

